206
00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:13.710
This film is credited as being written and directed by the Wachowski brothers.

207
00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:19.250
However, in the years since the movie franchise came out, both have come out as trans women.

208
00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:22.530
They are Lana Wachowski and Lily Wachowski.

209
00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:33.590
And in 2020, Lily Wachowski did an interview with Netflix Film Club, and she said that the Matrix films were an allegory for the transgender narrative.

210
00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:34.650
Here's a clip.

211
00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:44.190
We had, you know, the Matrix stuff was all like about the desire for transformation, but it was all coming from a closeted point of view.

212
00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:53.310
And so we had the character of Switch who was like a character who would be, you know, a man in the real world or and then a woman in the Matrix.

213
00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:59.910
And, you know, that's both were where our head spaces were.

214
00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:06.010
So, you know, ultimately, the character Switch does not change from male to female.

215
00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:08.430
I guess the studio wasn't into that idea.

216
00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:14.490
But Lily said, quote, I'm glad that it has gotten out that this was the original intention,

217
00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:22.070
and I love how meaningful those films are to trans people and the way they come up to me and say, these movies changed my life.

218
00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:34.550
And, lady, I was deep diving this, and there is a great article from NPR that goes deeper into the significance of the Matrix movies for people in the transgender community.

219
00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.730
I found it to be really educational.

220
00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:39.350
We can link to it in our stories.

221
00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:43.370
And I just already love this movie so much.

222
00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:50.530
But then to hear the ways that it has comforted a marginalized community of people was really, really moving to me.

