Meet me in the warehouse, but watch out for the men in reception.

1037
00:42:07.380 --> 00:42:08.380
There's no men.

1038
00:42:08.520 --> 00:42:09.360
It was...

1039
00:42:30.030 --> 00:42:34.910
That is the name I allowed you to know me by while I watched over you, waiting for the

1040
00:42:34.910 --> 00:42:35.890
time to approach.

1041
00:42:36.350 --> 00:42:37.750
That time has come.

1042
00:42:38.550 --> 00:42:41.290
And now, you may know my real name.

1043
00:42:42.330 --> 00:42:42.890
Dorpheus.

1044
00:42:43.510 --> 00:42:44.070
Dorpheus?

1045
00:42:44.070 --> 00:42:45.830
I'm Morpheus' brother.

1046
00:42:49.220 --> 00:42:54.790
The Matrix isn't real.

1047
00:42:55.070 --> 00:43:00.230
It's a trilogy of flawless, life-changing films and an online game.

1048
00:43:00.530 --> 00:43:06.510
The first Matrix movie was a program written by my team to prepare people for the truth.

1049
00:43:06.690 --> 00:43:11.370
But then the machines countered with their own program to make it seem as if a peace was

1050
00:43:11.370 --> 00:43:11.930
achieved.

1051
00:43:12.130 --> 00:43:15.190
So, there is no peace?

1052
00:43:15.350 --> 00:43:16.350
There is not.

1053
00:43:16.730 --> 00:43:18.210
Oh, that is terrible news.

1054
00:43:18.210 --> 00:43:19.490
Dwight, we need your help.

1055
00:43:19.750 --> 00:43:26.430
I would like you to join my underground army and help us wage war for the freedom of all

1056
00:43:26.430 --> 00:43:27.230
humankind.

1057
00:43:28.150 --> 00:43:29.530
Hank is good on his feet.

1058
00:43:29.730 --> 00:43:29.910
Right?

1059
00:43:30.110 --> 00:43:31.250
I told you he'd nail it.

1060
00:43:34.450 --> 00:43:38.230
If you take the blue pill, you will stay in the Matrix.

1061
00:43:38.630 --> 00:43:40.630
You will remember none of this.

1062
00:43:40.970 --> 00:43:42.790
Life will go on as it is for you.

1063
00:43:43.830 --> 00:43:51.810
If you take the red pill, I will open your eyes and you will see just how deep the rabbit

1064
00:43:51.810 --> 00:43:52.610
hole goes.

1065
00:43:56.250 --> 00:43:57.530
I'll take the blue pill.

1066
00:43:58.490 --> 00:44:02.510
Wait, now the blue will keep you in the program.

1067
00:44:02.870 --> 00:44:04.250
The red's the cool one.

1068
00:44:04.350 --> 00:44:04.850
I understand.

1069
00:44:04.850 --> 00:44:05.930
I'd like the blue pill, please.

1070
00:44:06.610 --> 00:44:07.930
Well, maybe I didn't explain myself.

1071
00:44:07.930 --> 00:44:09.650
Dorothy, you were very clear.

1072
00:44:09.850 --> 00:44:15.530
It's just, God, you know, I really appreciate the work that you and your brother are doing.

1073
00:44:16.090 --> 00:44:20.090
I appreciate it's too small a word, but the timing is terrible right now.

1074
00:44:20.310 --> 00:44:21.730
They just promoted me to manager.

1075
00:44:22.090 --> 00:44:23.450
Plus, I own this building.

1076
00:44:23.450 --> 00:44:24.950
I run a very substantial farm.

1077
00:44:25.110 --> 00:44:28.570
And I'm getting married soon to a woman I love.

1078
00:44:28.930 --> 00:44:34.390
And okay, yeah, maybe that love is just zeros and ones, but I don't want to lose it.

1079
00:44:35.330 --> 00:44:40.990
But no one hates machines more than me, but I'm happy.

1080
00:44:42.170 --> 00:44:43.810
I'm truly happy.

1081
00:44:44.650 --> 00:44:45.010
Aw.

1082
00:44:45.510 --> 00:44:46.830
Are you kidding me?

1083
00:44:46.930 --> 00:44:48.290
I hired 30 people.

1084
00:44:49.150 --> 00:44:50.590
The blue pill.

1085
00:44:50.590 --> 00:44:52.250
I did not see that coming.

1086
00:44:52.370 --> 00:44:53.010
I know.

1087
00:44:53.410 --> 00:44:56.610
Dwight takes the blue pill because he wants to stay happy.

1088
00:44:56.610 --> 00:44:58.030
He loves his life.

1089
00:44:58.390 --> 00:45:02.130
And, you know, you can hear Jim and Pam because they're watching it like on a monitor.

1090
00:45:02.350 --> 00:45:02.570
Yeah.

1091
00:45:02.570 --> 00:45:05.450
But yeah, it was an elaborate prank.

1092
00:45:05.630 --> 00:45:08.510
I mean, I don't know how much money Jim spent on that one.

1093
00:45:09.250 --> 00:45:10.130
Oh, yeah.

1094
00:45:10.430 --> 00:45:10.790
Uh-huh.

1095
00:45:11.290 --> 00:45:12.930
He hired 30 people.

1096
00:45:13.050 --> 00:45:13.710
30 people.

1097
00:45:14.010 --> 00:45:14.870
So there you go.

1098
00:45:15.010 --> 00:45:17.250
A little The Office, The Matrix crossover.

1099
00:45:17.750 --> 00:45:19.010
Well, I love that lady.

1100
00:45:19.430 --> 00:45:20.630
Why don't we take a break?

1101
00:45:21.070 --> 00:45:24.330
And when we come back, we'll talk about which pill Neo chose.

1102
00:45:24.710 --> 00:45:24.930
Yeah.

1103
00:45:35.080 --> 00:45:36.300
Everyone, we are back.

1104
00:45:36.440 --> 00:45:37.040
And guess what?

1105
00:45:37.940 --> 00:45:39.680
Neo takes the red pill.

1106
00:45:39.680 --> 00:45:40.360
Yeah.

1107
00:45:40.640 --> 00:45:46.400
And then Morpheus takes him into this sort of back room that's got a lot of computers and gadgets and stuff.

1108
00:45:46.400 --> 00:45:51.520
Yeah, they hook him up to, like, it seems like an EKG kind of a machine.

1109
00:45:51.880 --> 00:46:01.300
They're going to have to keep an eye on his vital signs because as this virtual world starts to break down in front of his eyes, like, literally, like,

1110
00:46:01.360 --> 00:46:03.980
the mirror becomes all gummy that he's looking at.

1111
00:46:03.980 --> 00:46:09.240
They need to make sure that he doesn't, like, freak himself out so much that he, like, goes into shock or something.

1112
00:46:09.440 --> 00:46:09.500
Yeah, exactly.

1113
00:46:09.500 --> 00:46:10.360
And his heart stops.

1114
00:46:10.620 --> 00:46:14.240
Well, Morpheus says, look, the pill you took is part of a tracing program.

1115
00:46:14.640 --> 00:46:21.880
It's designed to disrupt your input-output carrier signals so they can pinpoint his location in the pod field.

1116
00:46:22.700 --> 00:46:23.800
The pod field.

1117
00:46:23.880 --> 00:46:24.220
Mm-hmm.

1118
00:46:24.220 --> 00:46:26.800
Yeah, because that's where he really is.

1119
00:46:26.840 --> 00:46:31.560
And we're going to see him wake up in this pod of goo.

1120
00:46:31.740 --> 00:46:34.760
Of goo with all these tubes and—

1121
00:46:34.760 --> 00:46:35.660
He's naked.

1122
00:46:35.900 --> 00:46:36.560
He's naked.

1123
00:46:36.880 --> 00:46:38.180
This scene is so amazing.

1124
00:46:38.460 --> 00:46:41.000
It's something I still think about, like, this scene.

1125
00:46:41.300 --> 00:46:41.720
Yeah.

1126
00:46:41.720 --> 00:46:52.140
I mean, this big mechanical bug comes over, and it starts to, like, choke him, but then it starts—all the tubes that are attached to him start popping off.

1127
00:46:52.300 --> 00:46:52.980
Oh, baby.

1128
00:46:53.200 --> 00:46:56.980
And listen, I know that I said I wasn't going to look stuff up, but I looked this up.

1129
00:46:57.080 --> 00:46:59.580
Me too, because the scene is just bonkers.

1130
00:46:59.740 --> 00:47:00.500
It's so cool.

1131
00:47:00.720 --> 00:47:05.540
Did you watch the YouTube video about how they did this scene?

1132
00:47:05.540 --> 00:47:06.900
Did we watch the same thing?

1133
00:47:06.920 --> 00:47:07.600
I think we did.

1134
00:47:07.720 --> 00:47:08.700
With the water slide?

1135
00:47:08.880 --> 00:47:09.880
They built a slide.

1136
00:47:09.880 --> 00:47:13.900
I just want to share what a phenomenal physical actor Keanu is.

1137
00:47:13.980 --> 00:47:15.040
Oh, yeah, that's him in the pod.

1138
00:47:15.220 --> 00:47:16.120
That's him in the pod.

1139
00:47:16.480 --> 00:47:19.620
That spider thing that detaches him didn't exiSt.

1140
00:47:19.840 --> 00:47:23.240
Was it—there wasn't even, like, a thing with tennis balls on it.

1141
00:47:23.360 --> 00:47:23.540
Yeah.

1142
00:47:23.780 --> 00:47:26.100
There was nothing grabbing his neck at all.

1143
00:47:26.200 --> 00:47:30.320
He just is reacting, like, they're calling out different things for him.

1144
00:47:30.400 --> 00:47:31.800
He's reacting to nothing.

1145
00:47:32.120 --> 00:47:32.240
Yeah.

1146
00:47:32.360 --> 00:47:35.400
Even so much so, like, when he grabs, like, around his neck.

1147
00:47:35.580 --> 00:47:35.700
Yeah.

1148
00:47:35.720 --> 00:47:37.400
When it claws around his neck.

1149
00:47:37.520 --> 00:47:38.460
Yeah, that's what I was saying.

1150
00:47:38.460 --> 00:47:39.540
He's grabbing nothing.

1151
00:47:39.880 --> 00:47:44.480
And the whole time he's in this pod and they're doing different takes, there's someone with

1152
00:47:44.480 --> 00:47:48.760
a bucket, a literal bucket of clear goo that they're dumping on him.

1153
00:47:48.900 --> 00:47:50.820
Yeah, they're just slopping the goo back on.

1154
00:47:51.040 --> 00:47:57.680
Did you read that Keanu shaved his entire body, including his eyebrows, and lost 15 pounds

1155
00:47:57.680 --> 00:47:59.260
for this part of the movie?

1156
00:47:59.440 --> 00:48:00.260
Yes, I did.

1157
00:48:00.940 --> 00:48:01.860
That's crazy.

1158
00:48:02.120 --> 00:48:06.000
And that this scene concluded principal photography for the movie.

1159
00:48:06.180 --> 00:48:07.160
Well, that makes sense.

1160
00:48:07.160 --> 00:48:09.260
Yeah, because he had to shave his body.

1161
00:48:09.480 --> 00:48:09.800
Yeah.

1162
00:48:10.160 --> 00:48:13.140
And he really went down the tube into the water.

1163
00:48:13.380 --> 00:48:14.580
They made this whole water slide.

1164
00:48:14.620 --> 00:48:18.280
And when I was watching it, I was like, wait, two people come out the bottom.

1165
00:48:18.540 --> 00:48:21.620
Keanu and then a guy with a camera, I think.

1166
00:48:21.860 --> 00:48:26.160
Like, there was a cameraman who went down the slide with him, which is crazy.

1167
00:48:26.340 --> 00:48:26.780
Amazing.

1168
00:48:26.780 --> 00:48:29.060
I mean, how was your day at work, babe?

1169
00:48:29.340 --> 00:48:31.420
I went down a goo slide.

1170
00:48:31.720 --> 00:48:33.060
So here's the thing.

1171
00:48:33.280 --> 00:48:35.100
There's all this physicality happening.

1172
00:48:35.440 --> 00:48:42.200
But at the same time, there's also this real realization as he looks over the edge and he

1173
00:48:42.200 --> 00:48:45.320
sees pod after pod after pod.

1174
00:48:45.520 --> 00:48:47.780
And these machines kind of tending to them.

1175
00:48:47.980 --> 00:48:49.560
There's little tiny spider ones.

1176
00:48:49.720 --> 00:48:50.720
There's the big ones.

1177
00:48:50.900 --> 00:48:51.160
Yeah.

1178
00:48:51.160 --> 00:48:55.060
It's like a whole system of machines harvesting humans.

1179
00:48:55.880 --> 00:49:00.260
And I found this really great account called The Art of Storytelling.

1180
00:49:00.780 --> 00:49:02.600
And he sums up this moment.

1181
00:49:02.600 --> 00:49:04.000
And I want to share it with you.

1182
00:49:04.340 --> 00:49:04.580
Okay.

1183
00:49:04.580 --> 00:49:12.540
Quote, so in the span of two and a half minutes, we've witnessed the birth of a prophet, a nightmarish

1184
00:49:12.540 --> 00:49:18.860
vision of man's self-destruction, and a fragile hope for the salvation of humanity, all without

1185
00:49:18.860 --> 00:49:25.160
a single word of dialogue, relying only on the artistry and ingenuity of production designers,

1186
00:49:25.680 --> 00:49:30.860
VFX artists, musicians, sound designers, editors, and of course, the incredible dedication

1187
00:49:30.860 --> 00:49:32.080
of Keanu Reeves.

1188
00:49:32.080 --> 00:49:37.820
If this scene isn't a masterclass in how to affect an audience using the medium of cinema,

1189
00:49:38.040 --> 00:49:38.920
I don't know what is.

1190
00:49:39.180 --> 00:49:39.700
Mic drop.

1191
00:49:39.920 --> 00:49:42.540
Great YouTube summary of the scene I'll share in our stories.

1192
00:49:42.980 --> 00:49:46.260
Well, now Neo is brought aboard a ship.

1193
00:49:46.520 --> 00:49:47.860
This is the real world.

1194
00:49:48.000 --> 00:49:50.180
He's greeted by Morpheus and Trinity.

1195
00:49:50.520 --> 00:49:52.360
And, you know, he's like, am I dead?

1196
00:49:52.560 --> 00:49:53.800
And they're like, you're not dead.

1197
00:49:54.080 --> 00:49:54.480
Yeah.

1198
00:49:54.680 --> 00:49:57.960
The ship is the Nebuchadnezzar, which means protect my air.

1199
00:49:58.140 --> 00:49:58.540
Okay.

1200
00:49:58.980 --> 00:49:59.640
How about that?

1201
00:49:59.720 --> 00:50:01.720
He has to get strong.

1202
00:50:02.080 --> 00:50:04.300
He's going to get so much acupuncture.

1203
00:50:04.500 --> 00:50:08.540
You've never seen someone with so much acupuncture in your life.

1204
00:50:08.680 --> 00:50:09.880
They're rebuilding his muscles.

1205
00:50:10.040 --> 00:50:10.720
They've atrophied.

1206
00:50:10.880 --> 00:50:12.420
I've been getting acupuncture, lady.

1207
00:50:12.660 --> 00:50:14.040
You really love it.

1208
00:50:14.120 --> 00:50:14.740
You should share.

1209
00:50:15.060 --> 00:50:15.440
For my hot flashes.

1210
00:50:15.920 --> 00:50:21.740
Okay, because I'm taking tamoxifen for my breast cancer treatment, and a big side effect is hot flashes.

1211
00:50:21.740 --> 00:50:23.920
And I can't take anything for them.

1212
00:50:24.060 --> 00:50:27.820
When you go into menopause, you can do, like, hormone replacement therapy.

1213
00:50:27.820 --> 00:50:28.780
I can't.

1214
00:50:28.880 --> 00:50:34.500
The whole point of the medicine I'm taking is to unreplace my hormones, right?

1215
00:50:34.580 --> 00:50:36.080
To suppress my estrogen.

1216
00:50:36.380 --> 00:50:40.360
So I am white-knuckling my way through this, and the hot flashes are so bad.

1217
00:50:40.500 --> 00:50:44.920
And I started going to acupuncture, and I love it.

1218
00:50:44.920 --> 00:50:46.660
You said they've, like, stopped.

1219
00:50:46.840 --> 00:50:47.980
They have stopped.

1220
00:50:48.380 --> 00:50:48.860
Stopped.

1221
00:50:48.880 --> 00:50:49.320
That's crazy.

1222
00:50:49.320 --> 00:50:53.640
I used to wake up four to five times a night completely drenched.

1223
00:50:53.940 --> 00:50:55.360
So I'm sitting there.

1224
00:50:55.460 --> 00:51:00.660
I'm watching Neo with his 25,000 acupuncture needles, and I'm thinking,

1225
00:51:00.800 --> 00:51:02.620
Neo, you're going to be great.

1226
00:51:02.820 --> 00:51:04.360
This is going to work out for you.

1227
00:51:04.500 --> 00:51:05.220
Trust me.

1228
00:51:05.220 --> 00:51:05.600
Trust me.

1229
00:51:05.900 --> 00:51:07.380
And you're not going to have hot flashes.

1230
00:51:07.520 --> 00:51:08.660
He's not going to have any.

1231
00:51:08.840 --> 00:51:10.900
He does say, why do my eyes hurt?

1232
00:51:11.040 --> 00:51:13.000
Because they've never seen anything before.

1233
00:51:13.000 --> 00:51:14.840
Morpheus says you've never used them before.

1234
00:51:15.000 --> 00:51:15.220
Yeah.

1235
00:51:15.440 --> 00:51:16.580
How crazy is that?

1236
00:51:16.720 --> 00:51:17.200
I know.

1237
00:51:17.520 --> 00:51:20.840
So now some time has passed, and Neo is going to wake up.

1238
00:51:20.980 --> 00:51:21.700
He's dressed.

1239
00:51:22.140 --> 00:51:24.440
He's on a cot of some sort.

1240
00:51:24.620 --> 00:51:26.720
And I have to say something here.

1241
00:51:26.900 --> 00:51:27.120
Okay.

1242
00:51:27.340 --> 00:51:32.060
So they can create so many things in this world.

1243
00:51:32.300 --> 00:51:33.300
Is it about his wardrobe?

1244
00:51:33.540 --> 00:51:35.680
Why can't they make a sweater without a hole in it?

1245
00:51:36.180 --> 00:51:36.840
I think.

1246
00:51:36.920 --> 00:51:37.100
Why?

1247
00:51:37.120 --> 00:51:42.300
I said, why does everyone have, like, an old pair of long johns,

1248
00:51:42.300 --> 00:51:45.640
like, kind of waffle-y, long sleeve, and they all have holes?

1249
00:51:45.840 --> 00:51:48.180
This was my big complaint about The Last of Us.

1250
00:51:48.440 --> 00:51:51.300
This was very hard for me on The Last of Us.

1251
00:51:51.400 --> 00:51:56.000
I understand that the virus, you know, took over,

1252
00:51:56.040 --> 00:51:59.200
and we've had to sort of, like, live behind walls

1253
00:51:59.200 --> 00:52:00.860
in these little makeshift communities.

1254
00:52:00.860 --> 00:52:05.840
But did we lose our ability to sweep a floor or dust a shelf?

1255
00:52:05.840 --> 00:52:11.360
But, by the way, we have made matching outfits for people in the government

1256
00:52:11.360 --> 00:52:12.220
and our new government.

1257
00:52:12.220 --> 00:52:14.360
And we've made new currency.

1258
00:52:14.360 --> 00:52:15.060
Okay, okay.

1259
00:52:15.160 --> 00:52:17.000
And all kinds of badges and things.

1260
00:52:17.100 --> 00:52:17.380
Where?

1261
00:52:17.520 --> 00:52:18.720
Where are we making those?

1262
00:52:18.900 --> 00:52:22.200
And yet, in the place that we're living all the time,

1263
00:52:22.340 --> 00:52:23.760
no one swept a floor.

1264
00:52:24.180 --> 00:52:25.000
I didn't get it.

1265
00:52:25.160 --> 00:52:25.740
Like, why?

1266
00:52:25.960 --> 00:52:27.440
Everything was—it was so dirty.

1267
00:52:27.700 --> 00:52:28.200
No, I know.

1268
00:52:28.300 --> 00:52:29.000
You know what I'm saying?

1269
00:52:29.000 --> 00:52:30.940
And, by the way, we're going to get to the food.

1270
00:52:31.040 --> 00:52:32.920
I have the same complaint about the food.

1271
00:52:33.060 --> 00:52:34.120
There's no sun.

1272
00:52:35.840 --> 00:52:38.500
We have access, I think, to animals, right?

1273
00:52:38.720 --> 00:52:39.340
Okay, maybe.

1274
00:52:39.500 --> 00:52:41.360
We don't know because we haven't seen Zion.

1275
00:52:41.660 --> 00:52:42.000
Right.

1276
00:52:42.160 --> 00:52:42.820
We don't know what's there.

1277
00:52:43.020 --> 00:52:46.480
Zion's in the middle of the earth where it's still warm, a little bit warm.

1278
00:52:46.640 --> 00:52:46.840
Yeah.

1279
00:52:47.060 --> 00:52:49.940
So, maybe they do have to recycle their clothes.

1280
00:52:50.120 --> 00:52:52.080
From back in yield and times.

1281
00:52:52.080 --> 00:52:52.860
Maybe so.

1282
00:52:53.460 --> 00:52:54.420
But still.

1283
00:52:54.840 --> 00:52:55.320
Well—

1284
00:52:55.320 --> 00:52:57.540
We can't darn a hole in a sweater.

1285
00:52:57.560 --> 00:52:58.800
Maybe we could sew.

1286
00:52:59.460 --> 00:53:00.300
That's what I mean.

1287
00:53:00.360 --> 00:53:04.820
We can't take our patches of fabric that we have left

1288
00:53:04.820 --> 00:53:06.560
and turn it into something better.

1289
